<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Floating Rhythm BaGua Updater</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#12384a;--sage:#547768;--paper:#f7f4eb;--gold:#d6ac65;--night:#213f58}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f8f5e9,#e5eaf0);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 Georgia,serif}.wrap{max-width:820px;margin:40px auto;padding:24px}.card{background:#fffdf7;border:1px solid #d8d6cc;border-radius:22px;padding:28px;box-shadow:0 16px 40px #12384a18}h1{font-size:clamp(34px,6vw,58px);font-weight:500;margin:0 0 8px}.sub{font-style:italic;margin:0 0 24px}.row{display:grid;gap:14px}.pick{display:block;border:2px dashed #8da79a;border-radius:16px;padding:22px;background:#f7f4eb}input{display:block;margin-top:10px;width:100%}button{border:0;border-radius:999px;padding:12px 20px;background:var(--sage);color:#fff;font:700 16px system-ui;cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:not-allowed}.status{min-height:26px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.details{margin-top:18px;padding:16px;border-radius:14px;background:var(--night);color:#fff}.details b{color:#f1cf86}.details ul{margin-bottom:0}.small{font:13px/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#537066}
</style>
</head>
<body><main class="wrap"><section class="card">
<h1>Floating Rhythm</h1><p class="sub">BaGua source-map updater</p>
<div class="row">
<label class="pick"><strong>Choose the current cumulative Floating Rhythm HTML</strong><input id="file" type="file" accept=".html,text/html"></label>
<button id="apply" type="button" disabled>Inject sourced BaGua records and download</button>
<div id="status" class="status" aria-live="polite">Waiting for the current HTML file.</div>
</div>
<div class="details"><b>This update replaces BaGua records for:</b><ul><li>Tiger</li><li>Bear</li><li>Dragon — Yellow Dragon Rolls Over</li><li>Snake — White Snake Spits Out Tongue</li><li>Monkey — White Ape Presents Peaches (primate analogue, explicitly labeled)</li><li>Horse</li><li>Lion</li><li>Eagle</li></ul></div>
<p class="small">Monkey is now updated with the complete White Ape Presents Peaches material, explicitly labeled as a primate analogue rather than a historical Monkey form. Crane remains unchanged. All non-BaGua content is preserved.</p>
</section></main>
<script>
(()=>{
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s), file=$('#file'), apply=$('#apply'), status=$('#status');
let chosen=null;
const records={
"Tiger|BaGua Zhang":{type:"three",start:"Begin on the circle in a BaGua scissors stance with the crown lifted, chest relaxed, back open, shoulders and elbows dropped, and weight clearly differentiated between full and empty. Turn the torso toward the circle center. Open both palms before the chest in Fierce Tiger Comes Out of the Mountain.",seq:["Establish Tang Ni Bu mud-treading steps and walk the circle continuously. Let the feet initiate, the waist coordinate, and the palms follow the whole-body turn.","Maintain Fierce Tiger Comes Out of the Mountain while walking: both palms remain open before the chest as the waist twists toward the circle center. Do not stop walking to display the posture.","Keep the body upright and mobile. Avoid double weighting, forward bending, or independent arm movement; let the root travel with the stepping center.","To change direction, settle clearly into the support leg, use Kou Bu to close toward the circle, then Bai Bu to open onto the new line. Keep the change compact and controlled.","Re-establish Fierce Tiger Comes Out of the Mountain toward the new circle center and continue Tang Ni Bu in the opposite direction."],end:"Finish still walking or settle from a completed circle step with Fierce Tiger Comes Out of the Mountain intact: palms open before the chest, torso turned inward, shoulders released, center protected, and weight clearly full and empty."},
"Bear|BaGua Zhang":{type:"three",start:"Begin on the circle in a broad but mobile BaGua stance. Keep the crown lifted, back open, shoulders dropped, and torso turned toward the center. Establish Black Bear Stretches Out Its Paw with the rear palm extending forward and the other arm supporting nearer the front of the body.",seq:["Begin Tang Ni Bu circle walking with deliberate, continuous steps and no pause between weight transfer and palm expression.","Maintain Black Bear Stretches Out Its Paw while the waist continues to coil toward the circle center. Let the extended palm remain supported by the back and stepping base.","Differentiate full and empty clearly; keep the body substantial without becoming double weighted or static.","Use Kou Bu and Bai Bu for the direction change, lowering the center through the legs rather than bending the torso forward.","Re-form Black Bear Stretches Out Its Paw toward the new center and continue walking in the opposite direction."],end:"Finish rooted yet mobile on the circle with Black Bear Stretches Out Its Paw established, upper back broad, shoulders settled, and the whole-body turn continuing through the waist."},
"Dragon|BaGua Zhang":{"type":"three","start":"Begin in continuous circle walking with clear full and empty weighting, crown lifted, shoulders released, and the waist already spiraling toward the circle center.","seq":["Yellow Dragon Rolls Over: from the circle, advance while turning through the waist and reorganizing the feet without losing the connected upper-body spiral.","Cross and coil: continue the waist turn as the feet reposition; one palm remains higher while the other supports lower, preserving opposition through the torso.","Raise and roll over: lift the leg within comfortable balance while the palms maintain an inward-and-outward wrapped relationship, then continue the turn rather than freezing at the raised-leg position.","Return toward the circle through the Ward-Off-like action described in the linked-palms form, letting the waist carry the palms back into a connected walking structure.","Practice the form on the opposite side by reversing right and left, then resume circle walking with the Dragon spiral intact."],"end":"Finish back on the circle, upright and mobile, with the waist still spiraling and the palms organized around the center rather than held as a static pose."},
"Snake|BaGua Zhang":{"type":"three","start":"Begin circle walking with the body upright, shoulders released, elbows weighted, and the palms connected to the waist turn. Keep the steps quiet and the center ready to lower without folding the torso.","seq":["White Snake Spits Out Tongue: commit the weight into the supporting leg and use the waist to turn the upper body while the forward palm begins its circling path.","Circle and coil: let the palm travel over the head as the waist continues turning; protect the chest with the other hand and maintain the wrapped, twisting quality through the torso.","Lower into the crouching-Tiger-related position shown in the linked-palms sequence, changing level through the legs rather than collapsing the spine.","Kou bu into the figure-eight relationship, continue turning, and step backward while the moving foot brushes past the ankle; keep the palms coordinated with the waist throughout the change.","Rise from the low action as one palm lifts above the head and the other protects the center, then pierce forward through the palm action without locking the elbow.","Return to the circle using the same mechanics as the Single Palm Change. Reverse right and left to perform White Snake Spits Out Tongue on the other side."],"end":"Resume continuous circle walking in a narrow, coiled structure with the center mobile, palms alive, and the Snake quality expressed through softness outside and a connected internal core."},
"Horse|BaGua Zhang":{type:"three",start:"Begin on the circle in a longer but controlled BaGua walking stance. Turn the torso toward the center, keep the spine upright, and establish clear full and empty weighting before advancing.",seq:["Walk with sustained Tang Ni Bu steps, keeping the pelvis level and the hands coordinated with the waist.","Enter the Returning the Body Palm sequence through Green Dragon Stretches Its Claws and Step Forward and Palm Strike.","Continue through Swallow Skims the Water and Green Dragon Leaves the Water while preserving mobile rooting.","Perform Running Horse Suddenly Turns Back by changing direction through the feet and waist: close with Kou Bu, turn the body, open with Bai Bu, and let the palms arrive with the new line rather than before it.","Continue through the remaining change and return to circle walking in the opposite direction."],end:"Finish traveling on the reversed circle with a long connected stride, upright body, center protected, and momentum sustained without rushing."},
"Lion|BaGua Zhang":{type:"three",start:"Begin on the circle with the torso turned inward and the body lowered only as far as the legs can support an upright spine. Form Lion Opens Its Mouth: one palm curves above the head while the other curves before the walking posture.",seq:["Establish Tang Ni Bu and walk continuously while maintaining Lion Opens Its Mouth.","Keep the upper and lower palms connected through the back and waist; avoid lifting the upper shoulder or separating the arms from the stepping body.","Maintain clear full and empty weighting so the lowered posture remains mobile rather than fixed.","Change direction with Kou Bu and Bai Bu, allowing the waist to turn the Lion posture as one connected frame.","Re-establish Lion Opens Its Mouth toward the new center and continue walking without rising out of the chosen level."],end:"Finish low, upright, and mobile with Lion Opens Its Mouth intact, one palm high, one forward, shoulders released, and attention directed toward the circle center."},
"Eagle|BaGua Zhang":{type:"three",start:"Begin in a basic circle-walking posture with the torso turned toward the center, shoulders relaxed, elbows weighted, and hands ready to open from the back. Establish continuous Tang Ni Bu before adding the named movement.",seq:["Walk the circle continuously, coordinating feet, waist, spine, and hands.","Enter the Seventh Palm Change frame: Green Dragon Stretches Its Claws → Point the Toe Kicking → Swallow Skims the Water → Python Overturns Its Body → White Snake Lies in the Grass.","Rise from the lowered change into Eagle Spreads Its Wings, opening through the upper back and arms while keeping the shoulders down and the stance clearly weighted.","Continue through Push the Mountain into the Sea, Sweep the Rider from His Saddle, and Conceal the Flowers under the Leaves.","Use Kou Bu and Bai Bu to complete the change, return to Green Dragon Stretches Its Claws, and resume the circle in the opposite direction."],end:"Finish on the reversed circle with the chest relaxed, upper back broad, palms connected to the moving center, and Eagle's expansion preserved without stiffness."},"Monkey|BaGua Zhang":{"type":"three","start":"Use the traditional White Ape material as a clearly labeled primate analogue for Floating Rhythm's Monkey day. Begin on the circle with an upright but spring-ready body, shoulders loose, and weight clearly differentiated between full and empty.","seq":["White Ape Presents Peaches: enter from the circle through the documented kou-bu direction change, allowing the waist and palms to turn together.","Separate and circle the arms as the body changes orientation, keeping the chest and back rounded enough to preserve mobility rather than stiffening into a display pose.","Bring both palms together and lift them before projecting them outward as the body changes level through the legs.","Continue the photographed sequence through the alternating low stance and single-leg balance actions, keeping each lift controlled and the standing knee soft.","Turn the palms inward so the Tiger's Mouth spaces face one another, then continue through the reorientation shown in the form and recover the circle-walking structure.","Reverse right and left to practice the form on the opposite side."],"end":"Finish back in mobile circle walking with the palms gathered and the center ready to redirect. Source note: White Ape is preserved as White Ape; Floating Rhythm uses it as related primate material rather than renaming it as a historical Monkey form."}
};
function replaceObjectByKey(src,key,obj){
 const needle='"'+key+'"'; let k=src.indexOf(needle); if(k<0) throw new Error('Could not find '+key);
 let colon=src.indexOf(':',k+needle.length); if(colon<0) throw new Error('Malformed record '+key);
 let start=src.indexOf('{',colon); if(start<0) throw new Error('Malformed object '+key);
 let depth=0,inStr=false,esc=false,end=-1;
 for(let i=start;i<src.length;i++){
   const ch=src[i];
   if(inStr){if(esc){esc=false}else if(ch==='\\'){esc=true}else if(ch==='"'){inStr=false}continue}
   if(ch==='"'){inStr=true;continue}
   if(ch==='{')depth++; else if(ch==='}'){depth--; if(depth===0){end=i+1;break}}
 }
 if(end<0) throw new Error('Unclosed record '+key);
 return src.slice(0,start)+JSON.stringify(obj)+src.slice(end);
}
file.addEventListener('change',()=>{chosen=file.files[0]||null;apply.disabled=!chosen;status.textContent=chosen?'Ready to update '+chosen.name+'.':'Waiting for the current HTML file.'});
apply.addEventListener('click',async()=>{
 if(!chosen)return; apply.disabled=true; status.textContent='Injecting sourced BaGua records…';
 try{
  let text=await chosen.text();
  for(const [key,obj] of Object.entries(records)) text=replaceObjectByKey(text,key,obj);
  text=text.replace('Traditional Xingyi and Bagua animal names vary by lineage; Floating Rhythm records for nontraditional animals are designed movement translations, not lineage claims.','Traditional Xingyi and Bagua animal names vary by lineage. Tiger, Bear, Dragon, Snake, Horse, Lion, and Eagle BaGua records incorporate named Cheng-style material from The Whirling Circles of Ba Gua Zhang; other nontraditional animal records remain designed movement translations, not lineage claims.');
  const blob=new Blob([text],{type:'text/html'}),a=document.createElement('a');
  a.href=URL.createObjectURL(blob);a.download='Floating_Rhythm_BaGua_LinkedPalms_Update.html';document.body.appendChild(a);a.click();a.remove();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000);
  status.textContent='Done. The updated Floating Rhythm HTML has been downloaded.';
 }catch(err){status.textContent='Update stopped: '+err.message;apply.disabled=false;}
});
})();
</script></body></html>
